{
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "orm-preflight",
          "version": "<version>",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "no-drop-and-recreate-column",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a column that is dropped and added again in the same migration, which deletes every value in it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-drop-and-recreate-column.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a column that is dropped and added again in the same migration, which deletes every value in it. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-drop-and-recreate-column.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "data-loss",
                "tags": [
                  "data-loss"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "possible-rename-data-loss",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Warns when a migration drops one column and adds a different one on the same table without copying data, which is what a renamed entity property produces."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/possible-rename-data-loss.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Warns when a migration drops one column and adds a different one on the same table without copying data, which is what a renamed entity property produces. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/possible-rename-data-loss.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "data-loss",
                "tags": [
                  "data-loss"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-drop-column",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a dropped column, which deletes its data and breaks application code that still uses it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-drop-column.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a dropped column, which deletes its data and breaks application code that still uses it. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-drop-column.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "data-loss",
                "tags": [
                  "data-loss"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-drop-table",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a dropped table, which deletes all of its rows and breaks application code that still uses it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-drop-table.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a dropped table, which deletes all of its rows and breaks application code that still uses it. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-drop-table.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "data-loss",
                "tags": [
                  "data-loss"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-truncate",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports `TRUNCATE` and `queryRunner.clearTable()`, which delete every row of a table."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-truncate.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports `TRUNCATE` and `queryRunner.clearTable()`, which delete every row of a table. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-truncate.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "data-loss",
                "tags": [
                  "data-loss"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-rename-column",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a renamed column, which breaks the previous version of the application while a deploy is in progress."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-rename-column.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a renamed column, which breaks the previous version of the application while a deploy is in progress. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-rename-column.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "deploy-safety",
                "tags": [
                  "deploy-safety"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-rename-table",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a renamed table, which breaks the previous version of the application while a deploy is in progress."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-rename-table.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a renamed table, which breaks the previous version of the application while a deploy is in progress. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-rename-table.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "deploy-safety",
                "tags": [
                  "deploy-safety"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "require-concurrent-index",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports `CREATE INDEX` without `CONCURRENTLY`, which blocks writes to the table while the index is built."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-concurrent-index.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports `CREATE INDEX` without `CONCURRENTLY`, which blocks writes to the table while the index is built. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-concurrent-index.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "concurrent-index-transaction",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports `CREATE INDEX`, `DROP INDEX`, or `REINDEX` with `CONCURRENTLY` in a place where PostgreSQL runs it inside a transaction, which makes the migration fail."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/concurrent-index-transaction.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports `CREATE INDEX`, `DROP INDEX`, or `REINDEX` with `CONCURRENTLY` in a place where PostgreSQL runs it inside a transaction, which makes the migration fail. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/concurrent-index-transaction.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-add-not-null-without-default",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a `NOT NULL` column added to an existing table without a default, which fails as soon as the table has rows."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-add-not-null-without-default.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a `NOT NULL` column added to an existing table without a default, which fails as soon as the table has rows. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-add-not-null-without-default.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-volatile-default",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a column added with a volatile default, or as a serial, identity, or stored generated column, which rewrites the whole table under an exclusive lock."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-volatile-default.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a column added with a volatile default, or as a serial, identity, or stored generated column, which rewrites the whole table under an exclusive lock. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-volatile-default.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-unsafe-column-type-change",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a column type change that rewrites the whole table while blocking reads and writes."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-unsafe-column-type-change.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a column type change that rewrites the whole table while blocking reads and writes. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-unsafe-column-type-change.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "require-not-valid-foreign-key",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a foreign key added to an existing table without `NOT VALID`, which blocks writes to both tables while every row is checked."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-not-valid-foreign-key.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a foreign key added to an existing table without `NOT VALID`, which blocks writes to both tables while every row is checked. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-not-valid-foreign-key.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-set-not-null",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports `SET NOT NULL` on an existing column, which scans the whole table while blocking reads and writes."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-set-not-null.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports `SET NOT NULL` on an existing column, which scans the whole table while blocking reads and writes. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-set-not-null.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "require-not-valid-check",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a CHECK constraint added to an existing table without `NOT VALID`, which checks every row while blocking reads and writes."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-not-valid-check.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a CHECK constraint added to an existing table without `NOT VALID`, which checks every row while blocking reads and writes. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-not-valid-check.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "require-concurrent-unique",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a unique constraint or primary key added to an existing table, which builds its index while blocking reads and writes."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-concurrent-unique.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a unique constraint or primary key added to an existing table, which builds its index while blocking reads and writes. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-concurrent-unique.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "require-concurrent-index-drop",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports `DROP INDEX` without `CONCURRENTLY`, which blocks reads and writes on the table while it waits and runs."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-concurrent-index-drop.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports `DROP INDEX` without `CONCURRENTLY`, which blocks reads and writes on the table while it waits and runs. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-concurrent-index-drop.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-blocking-maintenance",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports `VACUUM FULL`, `CLUSTER`, and `REINDEX` without `CONCURRENTLY`, which block the table for as long as they run."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-blocking-maintenance.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports `VACUUM FULL`, `CLUSTER`, and `REINDEX` without `CONCURRENTLY`, which block the table for as long as they run. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-blocking-maintenance.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "enum-value-used-in-same-transaction",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a new enum value that is used in the same transaction that adds it, which PostgreSQL rejects."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/enum-value-used-in-same-transaction.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a new enum value that is used in the same transaction that adds it, which PostgreSQL rejects. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/enum-value-used-in-same-transaction.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "require-lock-timeout",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a migration that changes an existing table without setting `lock_timeout` first, so a busy table can stall all its traffic."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-lock-timeout.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a migration that changes an existing table without setting `lock_timeout` first, so a busy table can stall all its traffic. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-lock-timeout.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": false,
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "unanalyzable-statement",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Warns about a statement orm-preflight could not read, so that nothing it cannot check passes silently."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/unanalyzable-statement.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Warns about a statement orm-preflight could not read, so that nothing it cannot check passes silently. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/unanalyzable-statement.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "correctness",
                "tags": [
                  "correctness"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "no-edit-applied-migration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a migration that already exists on the base branch and was changed, since the change will never reach databases where it already ran."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-edit-applied-migration.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a migration that already exists on the base branch and was changed, since the change will never reach databases where it already ran. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/no-edit-applied-migration.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "correctness",
                "tags": [
                  "correctness"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "require-down",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a migration whose `down()` is empty or missing, so reverting it changes nothing but still marks it as not applied."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-down.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a migration whose `down()` is empty or missing, so reverting it changes nothing but still marks it as not applied. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/require-down.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "correctness",
                "tags": [
                  "correctness"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "invalid-suppression",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a suppression comment that names no rule, an unknown rule, or gives no reason."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/invalid-suppression.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a suppression comment that names no rule, an unknown rule, or gives no reason. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/invalid-suppression.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "correctness",
                "tags": [
                  "correctness"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "typeorm/no-changecolumn-recreate",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports `queryRunner.changeColumn()` calls that make TypeORM drop and re-add the column, which deletes every value in it."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/typeorm/no-changecolumn-recreate.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports `queryRunner.changeColumn()` calls that make TypeORM drop and re-add the column, which deletes every value in it. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/typeorm/no-changecolumn-recreate.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "data-loss",
                "tags": [
                  "data-loss"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "typeorm/transaction-override-forbidden",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a migration that sets its `transaction` property while TypeORM runs migrations in transaction mode `\"all\"`, where TypeORM refuses to run any pending migration."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/typeorm/transaction-override-forbidden.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a migration that sets its `transaction` property while TypeORM runs migrations in transaction mode `\"all\"`, where TypeORM refuses to run any pending migration. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/typeorm/transaction-override-forbidden.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "correctness",
                "tags": [
                  "correctness"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "typeorm/invalid-migration-name",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports a migration whose name does not end with a 13-digit timestamp, which makes TypeORM refuse to load any migration."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/typeorm/invalid-migration-name.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports a migration whose name does not end with a 13-digit timestamp, which makes TypeORM refuse to load any migration. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/typeorm/invalid-migration-name.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "correctness",
                "tags": [
                  "correctness"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "typeorm/no-enum-recreate",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Reports TypeORM's way of changing an enum by recreating the type, which rewrites every table that uses it and fails if a row holds a removed value."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/typeorm/no-enum-recreate.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "Reports TypeORM's way of changing an enum by recreating the type, which rewrites every table that uses it and fails if a row holds a removed value. See https://github.com/sikandar100/orm-preflight/blob/main/docs/rules/typeorm/no-enum-recreate.md"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "enabled": true,
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "locking",
                "tags": [
                  "locking"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "no-drop-and-recreate-column",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "\"users\".\"name\" is dropped and re-added in the same migration. Every existing value in this column will be lost. Why: TypeORM drops and re-adds a column when its type or length changes, instead of changing it in place. The new column starts empty. Safe: Change the type in place: ALTER TABLE \"users\" ALTER COLUMN \"name\" TYPE varchar(255). Widening a varchar, or changing varchar to text, does not rewrite the table. For other type changes, add a new column, backfill it, switch the code, and drop the old column in a later release."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/migrations/1727100000000-WidenUserName.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 7,
                  "startColumn": 30
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "no-add-not-null-without-default",
          "ruleIndex": 9,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "\"users\".\"name\" is added as NOT NULL without a default. The migration fails as soon as \"users\" has any rows. Why: PostgreSQL fills a new column with its default for every existing row. With no default that value is NULL, which the NOT NULL constraint rejects. Safe: Add the column as nullable, backfill it in batches, then enforce NOT NULL without a long lock (see no-set-not-null). Or add it with a constant default, which PostgreSQL 11 and later add without rewriting the table."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/migrations/1727100000000-WidenUserName.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 8,
                  "startColumn": 30
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "require-down",
          "ruleIndex": 22,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
